{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_architecture", "label": "dead-drop architecture overview", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each layer only knows about the one below it. The application never names a transport, and the transport never sees plaintext. Flow: application to Workspace over a local socket (or nothing at all in proxy mode), Workspace to mailbox engine to transport manager to adapters to the same stack on another machine."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_protocol", "label": "@fyrlabs/dead-drop/protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decides what a message is: envelope shape, framing, encryption, chunking, the error model. Zero dependencies, zero policy. Knows nothing about transports, workspaces or applications."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_transport_sdk", "label": "@fyrlabs/dead-drop-transport-sdk", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The contract third-party adapters compile against. Deliberately tiny and deliberately stable: the only thing outside this repository that has to keep working across releases."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_core", "label": "@fyrlabs/dead-drop/core", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All policy: which transport carries a message, when to retry, when to give up, what to record. The mailbox engine and the transport manager live here."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_runtime", "label": "@fyrlabs/dead-drop/runtime", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Turns core into a product: workspaces, exposures, discovery, the control plane, plugin loading."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_sdk", "label": "@fyrlabs/dead-drop/sdk and @fyrlabs/dead-drop front doors", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The two public entry points applications use."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace", "label": "Workspace (request/response, pub/sub, RPC)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Top layer of the runtime, reached by the application over a local socket or directly in proxy mode. Knows only the mailbox engine below it."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_mailbox_engine", "label": "Mailbox engine", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Framing, chunking, ack, dedupe, redelivery and polling. Supplies the messaging semantics that store adapters do not have, so adapter authors do not each reimplement at-least-once delivery."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_transport_manager", "label": "Transport manager", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scoring, retry, circuit breaker, failover and health. The boundary above which nothing may name a transport."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_adapters", "label": "Adapters (filesystem, git, github, memory, third-party)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sit below the transport manager and carry bytes to the same stack on another machine. They never see plaintext."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_layering_rule", "label": "Nothing above the transport manager names a transport", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rule that keeps the layering honest. Application code cannot ask for 'the GitHub one'; if it could, transport independence would be a slogan rather than a property. The same reasoning forbids anything above the manager from reading policy.mode."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_store_transport", "label": "store transport kind", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "put, get, list, delete, optionally watch. Around 50 lines for a typical backend; the mailbox engine supplies the messaging semantics. Chosen because nearly everything people want to use (GitHub, GitLab, OneDrive, SharePoint, S3, Dropbox, a synced folder) is an object store with no delivery semantics, and making every adapter author reimplement polling, acknowledgement, deduplication and at-least-once delivery would put subtle bugs in someone else's package."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_native_transport", "label": "native transport kind", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The backend already is a message system: it sends and subscribes directly."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_adr0001", "label": "ADR 0001 (store and native transports)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Records why the original sketch, in which every adapter implements send, receive and acknowledgement, was the wrong shape and was changed."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_key_layout", "label": "Mailbox key layout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ws/<workspace>/inbox/<peer>/<messageId>.ddf for direct messages, topic/<channel>/<messageId>.ddf for broadcast, peers/<peer>.ddf for presence beacons, dead/<peer>/<messageId>.ddf for dead letters. Keys are readable, and time-sortable ids give rough FIFO for free."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_delete_is_acknowledgement", "label": "Delete is the acknowledgement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sending is a write; receiving is list, fetch, decode, hand to a handler, delete. That single choice is what gives at-least-once delivery over a store that has no concept of a message."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_broadcast_retention_reaper", "label": "Broadcast retention reaper and subscriber cursors", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Broadcast messages belong to every subscriber so nobody may delete them; subscribers keep a local cursor and ask for keys after it, and a retention reaper removes messages past the window. It takes age from the message id rather than the store's modification time, because plenty of backends do not report one and treating 'age unknown' as 'old enough to delete' would destroy messages other subscribers had not read."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_adaptive_polling", "label": "Adaptive polling with watch interrupt", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Speeds up to the minimum interval while traffic flows and backs off to the maximum when idle; a transport supporting watch interrupts the wait instead of polling at all. Polling a rate-limited API every 250ms forever is how a transport gets throttled."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_transport_scoring", "label": "Transport scoring (health 45, reliability 25, latency 20, rate-limit headroom 10)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every transport is scored 0..1. An open circuit breaker scores zero, so it is chosen only when nothing else exists."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_circuit_breaker", "label": "Circuit breaker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An open breaker forces a transport's score to zero rather than removing it outright, so it remains a last resort."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_retry_and_failover", "label": "Retry with jittered backoff, then failover", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An operation is retried on its chosen transport with exponential backoff and full jitter, then moved to the next. Failover is skipped for caller-side errors, which fail identically everywhere."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_policy_modes", "label": "Policy modes: score, failover, parallel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "score is the default and the healthiest wins; failover respects the operator's declared order even when it is objectively slower; parallel writes through everything, made safe by receiver deduplication."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_runwrite", "label": "runWrite single write entry point", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "How many transports carry a write is a policy question, so callers ask the manager for a write rather than choosing between one transport and all of them. Nothing above the manager reads policy.mode, for the same reason nothing above it names a transport."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_selection_governs_writes_only", "label": "Selection governs writes only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The mailbox polls every store transport each cycle, and so do discovery and queue depth, so a message is found wherever it was written."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_request_response", "label": "Request/response correlation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The runtime owns correlation. A request registers a pending promise keyed by its message id, sets a TTL equal to its timeout so it cannot outlive the caller's patience, and sends; the remote handler produces a response envelope carrying correlationId, which resolves the promise. A late response to a timed-out request is logged at debug and dropped, because that is normal, not an error."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_deaddroperror", "label": "Structured DeadDropError in responses", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Handler failures are marshalled into the response as a structured error, so NOT_FOUND for a missing channel and SERVICE_ERROR for a handler that threw arrive as distinguishable errors rather than strings to match on."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_proxy_mode", "label": "Proxy mode (ddrop expose / ddrop connect)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ddrop expose --target http://localhost:3000 --name my-api registers a handler on channel http/my-api; ddrop connect peer/my-api starts a local HTTP server that packs each request into an envelope, waits for the response, and unpacks it."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_length_prefixed_body", "label": "Length-prefixed JSON head with raw byte body", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HTTP bodies travel as raw bytes after a length-prefixed JSON head rather than base64 inside it, so proxying a 10 MB response costs 10 MB, not 13 MB."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_observability", "label": "Observability at the runtime/transport boundary", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Structured JSON logs with credential redaction by field name and by value pattern; counters, gauges and histograms with Prometheus text output and no client-library dependency; spans in a bounded ring buffer so ddrop can answer 'which hop was slow' without an external collector. Living at the boundary is what gives an application transport latency, retries, failovers and payload sizes without instrumenting anything."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_one_runtime_per_machine", "label": "One runtime per machine", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Polling is the scarce resource. A process per project multiplies requests against the same rate limits for no benefit. One runtime hosts many workspaces, each with its own keys, transports, mailbox and peer identity, sharing only the process and the log."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_architecture", "target": "docs_architecture_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_architecture", "target": "docs_architecture_transport_sdk", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_architecture", "target": "docs_architecture_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_architecture", "target": "docs_architecture_runtime", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_architecture", "target": "docs_architecture_sdk", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_workspace", "target": "docs_architecture_mailbox_engine", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_architecture_transport_manager", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_transport_manager", "target": "docs_architecture_adapters", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_core", "target": "docs_architecture_mailbox_engine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_core", "target": "docs_architecture_transport_manager", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_runtime", "target": "docs_architecture_workspace", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_runtime", "target": "docs_architecture_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_core", "target": "docs_architecture_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adapters", "target": "docs_architecture_transport_sdk", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_layering_rule", "target": "docs_architecture_transport_manager", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_layering_rule", "target": "docs_architecture_runwrite", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adr0001", "target": "docs_architecture_store_transport", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adr0001", "target": "docs_architecture_native_transport", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_store_transport", "target": "docs_architecture_mailbox_engine", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adapters", "target": "docs_architecture_store_transport", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adapters", "target": "docs_architecture_native_transport", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_architecture_key_layout", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_key_layout", "target": "docs_architecture_delete_is_acknowledgement", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_delete_is_acknowledgement", "target": "docs_architecture_store_transport", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_broadcast_retention_reaper", "target": "docs_architecture_key_layout", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_broadcast_retention_reaper", "target": "docs_architecture_delete_is_acknowledgement", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_broadcast_retention_reaper", "target": "docs_adr_0006_reaping_orphaned_inboxes_age_from_key", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_mailbox_engine", "target": "docs_architecture_adaptive_polling", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_adaptive_polling", "target": "docs_architecture_store_transport", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_transport_manager", "target": "docs_architecture_transport_scoring", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weig